Patch in operator_block:
```python
vny = (-1.0)**np.arange(1, mm+1)
i0 = mm//2
lam_fd_nyq = -(A_h@vny)[i0]/vny[i0]
lam_fem_nyq = -(L_h@vny)[i0]/vny[i0]
nyq_dev_fd = abs(lam_fd_nyq - 4/hh**2)/(4/hh**2)
nyq_dev_fem = abs(lam_fem_nyq - 12/hh**2)/(12/hh**2)
```
and rows store those devs (expect ~1e-16).

Also for the "central row" claim: since A and L_fem are applied to vny, the center row's value of A@vny is exactly -4/h²·(-1)^i0 for any row with full stencil (i.e., rows 1..m-2); L_fem center row = -12/h²·(-1)^i0 to roundoff because the contamination from boundary rows decays with distance; at the center (m/2 ~ 300 rows away) it's below double precision. Good.

